# ============================================================
# HRStudio360 - Environment Variables Configuration
# ============================================================
#
# IMPORTANT: This is a template file. DO NOT commit actual credentials!
# Copy this file to .env for local development.
#
# For Vercel deployment, add these variables in:
# Project Settings > Environment Variables
# https://vercel.com/[your-username]/hrstudio360/settings/environment-variables
#
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 
# Get these from your Supabase project dashboard:
# https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/cgqoazepziswoziybhiz/settings/api
#
# Project ID: cgqoazepziswoziybhiz
# Project URL: https://cgqoazepziswoziybhiz.supabase.co
#

# Supabase Project URL
# Format: https://[PROJECT_ID].supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://cgqoazepziswoziybhiz.supabase.co

# Supabase Anon/Public Key
# This is safe to use in frontend code - it's public
# RLS (Row Level Security) policies protect your data
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImNncW9hemVwemlzd296aXliaGl6Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NjE4NTgwNDEsImV4cCI6MjA3NzQzNDA0MX0.WGxrf8LVcSXVfRH1OM2mlnNJfxwWKP-PewgSeq_rHeM

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: Service Role Key (BACKEND ONLY - NEVER in frontend!)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for server-side operations that bypass RLS
# DO NOT add this to Vercel unless you have server-side functions
# VITE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Sentry Error Tracking & Performance Monitoring (Optional)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 
# Production monitoring for error tracking and performance insights
# Get your DSN from: https://sentry.io (Free tier available)
#
# Same DSN works for both frontend and backend
# SENTRY_DSN=https://your-key@o123456.ingest.sentry.io/987654
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://your-key@o123456.ingest.sentry.io/987654
#
# Optional: Enable Sentry in development mode (default: disabled)
# SENTRY_DEBUG=true
# VITE_SENTRY_DEBUG=true
#
# Optional: App version for release tracking
# VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0
#

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (Neon PostgreSQL)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Automatically provided by Replit for development
# For production, add your Neon database URL
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/database
#

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Email Service (Resend - Optional)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# For transactional emails (e.g., collaborator invitations)
# Get your API key from: https://resend.com
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_api_key_here
#

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Session Secret (Required for Production)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Generate a strong random secret for production deployments
# SESSION_SECRET=your-long-random-secret-here
#

# ============================================================
# Vercel Deployment Instructions
# ============================================================
#
# 1. Go to: https://vercel.com
# 2. Import your GitHub repository: robertsala/HRStudio360
# 3. In Project Settings, add these environment variables:
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# 4. Deploy!
#
# Your app will be live at: https://hrstudio360.vercel.app
# (or similar URL provided by Vercel)
#
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Development vs Production
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Same credentials work for both environments!
# No need to create separate Supabase projects for dev/prod
# unless you specifically want to separate your data.
#
# If you DO want separate environments:
# 1. Create a new Supabase project for production
# 2. Run all migrations from supabase/migrations/ folder
# 3. Use production credentials in Vercel
# 4. Use development credentials in local .env
#
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Troubleshooting
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Issue: "Database error saving new user"
# Solution: Make sure all migrations in supabase/migrations/ 
#           have been run on your Supabase project
#
# Issue: "Invalid API key"
# Solution: Double-check you copied the ANON key, not the 
#           SERVICE ROLE key from Supabase dashboard
#
# Issue: Changes not appearing after deploy
# Solution: Clear Vercel cache and redeploy, or check that
#           you're looking at the latest deployment URL
#
# Need help? Check the README.md or QUICK_START.md
#
# ============================================================
